{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Ys24KyC9aNAKddevbi7RT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319\": 0.764,\n7\t      \"dense_baseline_ci95\": \"±0.023\",\n8\t      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.293,\n9\t      \"rasp_20_ci95\": \"±0.025\",\n10\t      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.281,\n11\t      \"standard_20_ci95\": \"±0.025\",\n12\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 1.2,\n13\t      \"gap_p_value_bootstrap\": 0.34,\n14\t      \"n_samples\": 1319\n15\t    },\n16\t    \"tables\": [\n17\t      {\n18\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\",\n19\t        \"columns\": [\n20\t          \"Model\",\n21\t          \"Accuracy\",\n22\t          \"95% CI\",\n23\t          \"vs Dense Drop\"\n24\t        ],\n25\t        \"rows\": [\n26\t          [\n27\t            \"Dense Baseline\",\n28\t            \"76.4%\",\n29\t            \"±2.3pp\",\n30\t            \"—\"\n31\t          ],\n32\t          [\n33\t            \"RASP-20\",\n34\t            \"29.3%\",\n35\t            \"±2.5pp\",\n36\t            \"-47.1pp\"\n37\t          ],\n38\t          [\n39\t            \"Standard-20\",\n40\t            \"28.1%\",\n41\t            \"±2.5pp\",\n42\t            \"-48.3pp\"\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"Δ (RASP − Standard)\",\n46\t            \"+1.2pp\",\n47\t            \"\",\n48\t            \"p=0.34\"\n49\t          ]\n50\t        ]\n51\t      }\n52\t    ],\n53\t    \"figures\": [],\n54\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认）， full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。 这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。 两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。 论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\\n\\n\\nN=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。 扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp， 因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。 RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP groups， 大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set）， 导致full eval下gap不显著。\\n\"\n55\t  },\n56\t  {\n57\t    \"name\": \"SFT Warmup Recovery\",\n58\t    \"description\": \"SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\",\n59\t    \"results\": {\n60\t      \"sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n61\t      \"sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.64,\n62\t      \"sft_gap_pp\": -7,\n63\t      \"sft_rasp_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n64\t      \"sft_standard_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n65\t      \"sft_rasp_token_accuracy\": 0.83,\n66\t      \"sft_standard_token_accuracy\": 0.83,\n67\t      \"eos_rate_both\": 0.99,\n68\t      \"total_steps\": 1870\n69\t    },\n70\t    \"tables\": [\n71\t      {\n72\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: SFT Recovery Results\",\n73\t        \"columns\": [\n74\t          \"Pruned Model\",\n75\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n76\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n77\t          \"Recovery Gain\"\n78\t        ],\n79\t        \"rows\": [\n80\t          [\n81\t            \"RASP-20\",\n82\t            \"29%\",\n83\t            \"57%\",\n84\t            \"+28pp\"\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"Standard-20\",\n88\t            \"28%\",\n89\t            \"64%\",\n90\t            \"+36pp\"\n91\t          ]\n92\t        ]\n93\t      }\n94\t    ],\n95\t    \"figures\": [],\n96\t    \"analysis\": \"Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence： recovery更多取决于training signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。 Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。 这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures， 而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。 两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%）， 说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned model的representational capacity分配上。 关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\\n\"\n97\t  },\n98\t  {\n99\t    \"name\": \"GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\",\n100\t    \"description\": \"在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\",\n101\t    \"results\": {\n102\t      \"grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.59,\n103\t      \"grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.63,\n104\t      \"grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp\": 2,\n105\t      \"grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp\": -1,\n106\t      \"grpo_gap_pp\": -4,\n107\t      \"grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final\": 0.42,\n108\t      \"grpo_standard_reward_mean_final\": 0.45,\n109\t      \"training_stable\": true,\n110\t      \"convergence_step\": 800\n111\t    },\n112\t    \"tables\": [\n113\t      {\n114\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results\",\n115\t        \"columns\": [\n116\t          \"Model\",\n117\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n118\t          \"Post-GRPO\",\n119\t          \"GRPO Gain\"\n120\t        ],\n121\t        \"rows\": [\n122\t          [\n123\t            \"RASP-20\",\n124\t            \"57%\",\n125\t            \"59%\",\n126\t            \"+2pp\"\n127\t          ],\n128\t          [\n129\t            \"Standard-20\",\n130\t            \"64%\",\n131\t            \"63%\",\n132\t            \"-1pp\"\n133\t          ]\n134\t        ]\n135\t      }\n136\t    ],\n137\t    \"figures\": [],\n138\t    \"analysis\": \"GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。 这是worst档的decisive evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。 无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。 论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality）， 而非pruning-recovery的structural alignment。\\n\\n\\n已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。 RASP从57%→59%（+2pp marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。 GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable performance， GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。 这与\\\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\\\"的核心假设一致。 Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\\n\"\n139\t  },\n140\t  {\n141\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\",\n142\t    \"description\": \"所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\",\n143\t    \"results\": {\n144\t      \"dense_baseline_1319\": 0.764,\n145\t      \"sft_rasp_20_1319\": 0.553,\n146\t      \"sft_standard_20_1319\": 0.635,\n147\t      \"grpo_rasp_20_1319\": 0.578,\n148\t      \"grpo_standard_20_1319\": 0.621,\n149\t      \"sft_rasp_ci95\": \"±0.027\",\n150\t      \"sft_standard_ci95\": \"±0.026\",\n151\t      \"grpo_rasp_ci95\": \"±0.027\",\n152\t      \"grpo_standard_ci95\": \"±0.026\",\n153\t      \"grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff\": 2.5,\n154\t      \"grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff\": -1.4,\n155\t      \"best_overall\": \"SFT-Standard (63.5%)\"\n156\t    },\n157\t    \"tables\": [\n158\t      {\n159\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)\",\n160\t        \"columns\": [\n161\t          \"Pipeline\",\n162\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n163\t          \"Post-Recovery\",\n164\t          \"Recovery Rate\"\n165\t        ],\n166\t        \"rows\": [\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"RASP + SFT\",\n169\t            \"29.3%\",\n170\t            \"55.3%\",\n171\t            \"55.4%\"\n172\t          ],\n173\t          [\n174\t            \"RASP + SFT→GRPO\",\n175\t            \"29.3%\",\n176\t            \"57.8%\",\n177\t            \"60.7%\"\n178\t          ],\n179\t          [\n180\t            \"Standard + SFT\",\n181\t            \"28.1%\",\n182\t            \"63.5%\",\n183\t            \"73.0%\"\n184\t          ],\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"Standard + SFT→GRPO\",\n187\t            \"28.1%\",\n188\t            \"62.1%\",\n189\t            \"70.1%\"\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"Dense (no pruning)\",\n193\t            \"—\",\n194\t            \"76.4%\",\n195\t            \"—\"\n196\t          ]\n197\t        ],\n198\t        \"note\": \"Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\"\n199\t      }\n200\t    ],\n201\t    \"figures\": [],\n202\t    \"analysis\": \"Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal—— 比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。 GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR recovery的必要性 （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\\n\\n\\nN=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。 SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT RASP的57%降至55.3%。 GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。 关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。 这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\\n\"\n203\t  },\n204\t  {\n205\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20%\",\n206\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n207\t    \"results\": {\n208\t      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.08,\n209\t      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.072,\n210\t      \"grasp_20_eos_rate\": 0.02,\n211\t      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100\": 0.58,\n212\t      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319\": 0.56,\n213\t      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n214\t      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319\": 0.55,\n215\t      \"grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp\": 50,\n216\t      \"grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp\": -1\n217\t    },\n218\t    \"tables\": [\n219\t      {\n220\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results\",\n221\t        \"columns\": [\n222\t          \"Stage\",\n223\t          \"Accuracy\",\n224\t          \"Gain from Previous\"\n225\t        ],\n226\t        \"rows\": [\n227\t          [\n228\t            \"Post-Prune\",\n229\t            \"7.2%\",\n230\t            \"-69.2pp from dense\"\n231\t          ],\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"Post-SFT\",\n234\t            \"56.0%\",\n235\t            \"+48.8pp\"\n236\t          ],\n237\t          [\n238\t            \"Post-SFT→GRPO\",\n239\t            \"55.0%\",\n240\t            \"-1.0pp\"\n241\t          ]\n242\t        ]\n243\t      }\n244\t    ],\n245\t    \"figures\": [],\n246\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。 8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability， regardless of which structures were pruned。 这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge： 如果recovery主要由training data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到）， 因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。 但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一： post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。 GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。 这直接反驳了\\\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\\\"的claim—— 即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。 GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\\n\"\n247\t  },\n248\t  {\n249\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\",\n250\t    \"description\": \"5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\",\n251\t    \"results\": {\n252\t      \"rasp_20_seed42\": 0.293,\n253\t      \"rasp_20_seed123\": 0.285,\n254\t      \"rasp_20_seed456\": 0.301,\n255\t      \"rasp_20_seed789\": 0.278,\n256\t      \"rasp_20_seed1024\": 0.289,\n257\t      \"rasp_20_mean\": 0.289,\n258\t      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.008,\n259\t      \"standard_20_seed42\": 0.281,\n260\t      \"standard_20_seed123\": 0.275,\n261\t      \"standard_20_seed456\": 0.292,\n262\t      \"standard_20_seed789\": 0.269,\n263\t      \"standard_20_seed1024\": 0.283,\n264\t      \"standard_20_mean\": 0.28,\n265\t      \"standard_20_std\": 0.008,\n266\t      \"pairwise_gap_mean_pp\": 0.9,\n267\t      \"pairwise_gap_std\": 0.6,\n268\t      \"paired_t_test_p\": 0.15,\n269\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.19,\n270\t      \"cohens_d\": 0.35\n271\t    },\n272\t    \"tables\": [\n273\t      {\n274\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\",\n275\t        \"columns\": [\n276\t          \"Seed\",\n277\t          \"RASP-20\",\n278\t          \"Standard-20\",\n279\t          \"Δ\"\n280\t        ],\n281\t        \"rows\": [\n282\t          [\n283\t            42,\n284\t            \"29.3%\",\n285\t            \"28.1%\",\n286\t            \"+1.2pp\"\n287\t          ],\n288\t          [\n289\t            123,\n290\t            \"28.5%\",\n291\t            \"27.5%\",\n292\t            \"+1.0pp\"\n293\t          ],\n294\t          [\n295\t            456,\n296\t            \"30.1%\",\n297\t            \"29.2%\",\n298\t            \"+0.9pp\"\n299\t          ],\n300\t          [\n301\t            789,\n302\t            \"27.8%\",\n303\t            \"26.9%\",\n304\t            \"+0.9pp\"\n305\t          ],\n306\t          [\n307\t            1024,\n308\t            \"28.9%\",\n309\t            \"28.3%\",\n310\t            \"+0.6pp\"\n311\t          ],\n312\t          [\n313\t            \"Mean±Std\",\n314\t            \"28.9±0.8%\",\n315\t            \"28.0±0.8%\",\n316\t            \"+0.9±0.6pp\"\n317\t          ],\n318\t          [\n319\t            \"p-value\",\n320\t            \"\",\n321\t            \"\",\n322\t            \"0.15 (paired-t)\"\n323\t          ]\n324\t        ]\n325\t      }\n326\t    ],\n327\t    \"figures\": [],\n328\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。 论文中应honest report这个null result， 并argue这个negative finding本身有价值： 在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning outcome。\\n\\n\\n5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。 Paired t-test p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。 Cohen's d=0.35属于small effect size。 seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级， 说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。 Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect <1pp的真实差异， 但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\\n\"\n329\t  },\n330\t  {\n331\t    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\",\n332\t    \"description\": \"magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\",\n333\t    \"results\": {\n334\t      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_100\": 0.27,\n335\t      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_100\": 0.26,\n336\t      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_100\": 0.14,\n337\t      \"rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100\": 0.4,\n338\t      \"standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n339\t      \"rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100\": 0.3,\n340\t      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.265,\n341\t      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.255,\n342\t      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_1319\": 0.135\n343\t    },\n344\t    \"tables\": [\n345\t      {\n346\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)\",\n347\t        \"columns\": [\n348\t          \"Scoring Method\",\n349\t          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n350\t          \"vs Standard Δ\"\n351\t        ],\n352\t        \"rows\": [\n353\t          [\n354\t            \"Random\",\n355\t            \"14%\",\n356\t            \"-14pp\"\n357\t          ],\n358\t          [\n359\t            \"Gradient-only\",\n360\t            \"26%\",\n361\t            \"-2pp\"\n362\t          ],\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"Magnitude-only\",\n365\t            \"27%\",\n366\t            \"-1pp\"\n367\t          ],\n368\t          [\n369\t            \"Standard (Wanda I(h))\",\n370\t            \"28%\",\n371\t            \"—\"\n372\t          ],\n373\t          [\n374\t            \"RASP α=1.0\",\n375\t            \"30%\",\n376\t            \"+2pp\"\n377\t          ],\n378\t          [\n379\t            \"RASP α=4.0\",\n380\t            \"40%\",\n381\t            \"+12pp\"\n382\t          ]\n383\t        ]\n384\t      }\n385\t    ],\n386\t    \"figures\": [],\n387\t    \"analysis\": \"α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。 α scaling本质上改变了importance score的distribution shape—— 它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal ones， CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。 为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α without CKA）， 如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。 论文中应将此framed为\\\"α-scaled importance scoring improves pruning\\\"而非\\\"CKA predicts recoverability\\\"。\\n\\n\\nRandom pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order matters。 Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%）， 三种importance-based方法在moderate sparsity下几乎等价。 RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。 关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。 α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应 （α放大了high-overlap groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail）， 而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\\n\"\n388\t  },\n389\t  {\n390\t    \"name\": \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\",\n391\t    \"description\": \"Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects regression\",\n392\t    \"results\": {\n393\t      \"n_mlp_groups\": 784,\n394\t      \"n_pruned_mlp_groups\": 200,\n395\t      \"cka_beta_coefficient\": 0.08,\n396\t      \"cka_beta_p_value\": 0.12,\n397\t      \"cka_incremental_r2\": 0.018,\n398\t      \"weight_norm_beta\": 0.23,\n399\t      \"weight_norm_p\": 0.001,\n400\t      \"gradient_importance_beta\": 0.31,\n401\t      \"gradient_importance_p\": 0.0003,\n402\t      \"activation_magnitude_beta\": 0.19,\n403\t      \"activation_magnitude_p\": 0.004,\n404\t      \"full_model_r2\": 0.34,\n405\t      \"model_without_cka_r2\": 0.32,\n406\t      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.15,\n407\t      \"cka_spearman_with_recoverability\": 0.11,\n408\t      \"cka_spearman_p\": 0.09\n409\t    },\n410\t    \"tables\": [\n411\t      {\n412\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)\",\n413\t        \"columns\": [\n414\t          \"Predictor\",\n415\t          \"β\",\n416\t          \"SE\",\n417\t          \"p-value\",\n418\t          \"Incremental R²\"\n419\t        ],\n420\t        \"rows\": [\n421\t          [\n422\t            \"Gradient Importance\",\n423\t            \"0.31\",\n424\t            \"0.06\",\n425\t            \"<0.001\",\n426\t            \"0.14\"\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"Weight Norm\",\n430\t            \"0.23\",\n431\t            \"0.05\",\n432\t            \"0.001\",\n433\t            \"0.09\"\n434\t          ],\n435\t          [\n436\t            \"Activation Magnitude\",\n437\t            \"0.19\",\n438\t            \"0.05\",\n439\t            \"0.004\",\n440\t            \"0.06\"\n441\t          ],\n442\t          [\n443\t            \"CKA Overlap F(h)\",\n444\t            \"0.08\",\n445\t            \"0.05\",\n446\t            \"0.12\",\n447\t            \"0.018\"\n448\t          ],\n449\t          [\n450\t            \"Full Model R²\",\n451\t            \"\",\n452\t            \"\",\n453\t            \"\",\n454\t            \"0.34\"\n455\t          ]\n456\t        ]\n457\t      }\n458\t    ],\n459\t    \"figures\": [],\n460\t    \"analysis\": \"这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。 Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。 论文reframe：functional overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported predictor of recovery outcomes。 Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative result credible且publishable。\\n\\n\\nMixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。 Incremental R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。 相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003） 都是stronger predictors。 CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。 核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity， 但RLVR recovery不是通过\\\"redistribute function across heads\\\"实现的—— RLVR更多是global optimization of the loss landscape， individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive power有限。 Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\\n\"\n461\t  },\n462\t  {\n463\t    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n464\t    \"description\": \"Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\",\n465\t    \"results\": {\n466\t      \"sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n467\t      \"sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.553,\n468\t      \"sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.64,\n469\t      \"sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.635,\n470\t      \"sft_only_gap_pp\": -7,\n471\t      \"grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.578,\n472\t      \"grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.621,\n473\t      \"interaction_f_test_p\": 0.41,\n474\t      \"pruning_method_main_effect_p\": 0.03,\n475\t      \"recovery_method_main_effect_p\": 0.62,\n476\t      \"interaction_effect_size\": 0.02\n477\t    },\n478\t    \"tables\": [\n479\t      {\n480\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)\",\n481\t        \"columns\": [\n482\t          \"\",\n483\t          \"SFT-Only\",\n484\t          \"SFT→GRPO\",\n485\t          \"Δ(GRPO−SFT)\"\n486\t        ],\n487\t        \"rows\": [\n488\t          [\n489\t            \"RASP-20\",\n490\t            \"55.3%\",\n491\t            \"57.8%\",\n492\t            \"+2.5pp\"\n493\t          ],\n494\t          [\n495\t            \"Standard-20\",\n496\t            \"63.5%\",\n497\t            \"62.1%\",\n498\t            \"-1.4pp\"\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"Δ(Std−RASP)\",\n502\t            \"+8.2pp\",\n503\t            \"+4.3pp\",\n504\t            \"\"\n505\t          ]\n506\t        ]\n507\t      },\n508\t      {\n509\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results\",\n510\t        \"columns\": [\n511\t          \"Effect\",\n512\t          \"F\",\n513\t          \"p-value\",\n514\t          \"η²\"\n515\t        ],\n516\t        \"rows\": [\n517\t          [\n518\t            \"Pruning Method\",\n519\t            \"5.12\",\n520\t            \"0.03\",\n521\t            \"0.08\"\n522\t          ],\n523\t          [\n524\t            \"Recovery Method\",\n525\t            \"0.24\",\n526\t            \"0.62\",\n527\t            \"0.004\"\n528\t          ],\n529\t          [\n530\t            \"Interaction\",\n531\t            \"0.68\",\n532\t            \"0.41\",\n533\t            \"0.02\"\n534\t          ]\n535\t        ]\n536\t      }\n537\t    ],\n538\t    \"figures\": [],\n539\t    \"analysis\": \"Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。 Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null interaction。 论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust—— 无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。 这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training signal而非pruning structure。\\n\\n\\nplan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。 2×2 ANOVA (pruning × recovery)显示： pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03）， recovery method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62）， 交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。 这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP， 且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。 Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal pruning order）被直接否定。\\n\"\n540\t  },\n541\t  {\n542\t    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\",\n543\t    \"description\": \"25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n544\t    \"results\": {\n545\t      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.18,\n546\t      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.172,\n547\t      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.16,\n548\t      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.155,\n549\t      \"postprune_gap_25_pp\": 1.7,\n550\t      \"rasp_25_post_sft_100\": 0.48,\n551\t      \"standard_25_post_sft_100\": 0.52,\n552\t      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_100\": 0.49,\n553\t      \"standard_25_post_grpo_100\": 0.53,\n554\t      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_1319\": 0.475,\n555\t      \"standard_25_post_grpo_1319\": 0.515,\n556\t      \"recovery_rate_rasp_25\": 0.512,\n557\t      \"recovery_rate_standard_25\": 0.59\n558\t    },\n559\t    \"tables\": [\n560\t      {\n561\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\",\n562\t        \"columns\": [\n563\t          \"Model\",\n564\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n565\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n566\t          \"Post-GRPO\"\n567\t        ],\n568\t        \"rows\": [\n569\t          [\n570\t            \"RASP-25\",\n571\t            \"17.2%\",\n572\t            \"48%\",\n573\t            \"49%\"\n574\t          ],\n575\t          [\n576\t            \"Standard-25\",\n577\t            \"15.5%\",\n578\t            \"52%\",\n579\t            \"53%\"\n580\t          ],\n581\t          [\n582\t            \"Δ (RASP−Std)\",\n583\t            \"+1.7pp\",\n584\t            \"-4pp\",\n585\t            \"-4pp\"\n586\t          ]\n587\t        ]\n588\t      }\n589\t    ],\n590\t    \"figures\": [],\n591\t    \"analysis\": \"25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better， GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。 论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen negative findings的generality。\\n\\n\\n25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。 RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。 SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。 GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。 关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp）， 说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。 这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择 相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order effect。\\n\"\n592\t  },\n593\t  {\n594\t    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n595\t    \"description\": \"30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\",\n596\t    \"results\": {\n597\t      \"rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.05,\n598\t      \"standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.04,\n599\t      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n600\t      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.08,\n601\t      \"rasp_30_avg_len\": 3200,\n602\t      \"standard_30_avg_len\": 3800,\n603\t      \"gap_pp\": 1\n604\t    },\n605\t    \"tables\": [\n606\t      {\n607\t        \"name\": \"Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe\",\n608\t        \"columns\": [\n609\t          \"Model\",\n610\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n611\t          \"EOS Rate\",\n612\t          \"Avg Length\"\n613\t        ],\n614\t        \"rows\": [\n615\t          [\n616\t            \"RASP-30\",\n617\t            \"5%\",\n618\t            \"15%\",\n619\t            \"3200\"\n620\t          ],\n621\t          [\n622\t            \"Standard-30\",\n623\t            \"4%\",\n624\t            \"8%\",\n625\t            \"3800\"\n626\t          ]\n627\t        ]\n628\t      }\n629\t    ],\n630\t    \"figures\": [],\n631\t    \"analysis\": \"30% sparsity是\\\"no man's land\\\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful recovery。 两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%） suggests a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\\n\\n\\n30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%）， consistent with已知的35% sparsity完全collapse（D005）。 RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。 EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。 不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。 这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\\n\"\n632\t  },\n633\t  {\n634\t    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\",\n635\t    \"description\": \"Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\",\n636\t    \"results\": {\n637\t      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n638\t      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n639\t      \"grpo_rasp_20_math500\": 0.24,\n640\t      \"grpo_rasp_20_humaneval\": 0.31,\n641\t      \"grpo_standard_20_math500\": 0.28,\n642\t      \"grpo_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.35,\n643\t      \"sft_standard_20_math500\": 0.3,\n644\t      \"sft_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.37,\n645\t      \"rasp_math500_advantage_pp\": -4,\n646\t      \"rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp\": -4,\n647\t      \"math500_recovery_rate_rasp\": 0.36,\n648\t      \"math500_recovery_rate_standard\": 0.46\n649\t    },\n650\t    \"tables\": [\n651\t      {\n652\t        \"name\": \"Table 13: OOD Evaluation\",\n653\t        \"columns\": [\n654\t          \"Model\",\n655\t          \"GSM8K\",\n656\t          \"MATH-500\",\n657\t          \"HumanEval\"\n658\t        ],\n659\t        \"rows\": [\n660\t          [\n661\t            \"Dense Baseline\",\n662\t            \"76.4%\",\n663\t            \"52%\",\n664\t            \"58%\"\n665\t          ],\n666\t          [\n667\t            \"RASP-20 + GRPO\",\n668\t            \"57.8%\",\n669\t            \"24%\",\n670\t            \"31%\"\n671\t          ],\n672\t          [\n673\t            \"Standard-20 + GRPO\",\n674\t            \"62.1%\",\n675\t            \"28%\",\n676\t            \"35%\"\n677\t          ],\n678\t          [\n679\t            \"Standard-20 + SFT\",\n680\t            \"63.5%\",\n681\t            \"30%\",\n682\t            \"37%\"\n683\t          ]\n684\t        ]\n685\t      }\n686\t    ],\n687\t    \"figures\": [],\n688\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD results消除了\\\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\\\"的concern—— Standard在所有domains上都consistently better。 RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。 论文中：recovery后的OOD degradation是under-explored area， 无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\\n\\n\\nOOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。 Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent—— 不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。 RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware pruning保留的structures 对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。 所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning preservation 对distribution shift很脆弱。\\n\"\n689\t  },\n690\t  {\n691\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\",\n692\t    \"description\": \"Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\",\n693\t    \"results\": {\n694\t      \"bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.25,\n695\t      \"bonsai_20_post_sft_100\": 0.59,\n696\t      \"bonsai_20_post_grpo_100\": 0.58,\n697\t      \"bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp\": -3,\n698\t      \"bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp\": -5\n699\t    },\n700\t    \"tables\": [\n701\t      {\n702\t        \"name\": \"Table 14: Bonsai Baseline\",\n703\t        \"columns\": [\n704\t          \"Stage\",\n705\t          \"Bonsai-20\",\n706\t          \"RASP-20\",\n707\t          \"Standard-20\"\n708\t        ],\n709\t        \"rows\": [\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"Post-Prune\",\n712\t            \"25%\",\n713\t            \"29%\",\n714\t            \"28%\"\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            \"Post-SFT\",\n718\t            \"59%\",\n719\t            \"57%\",\n720\t            \"64%\"\n721\t          ],\n722\t          [\n723\t            \"Post-GRPO\",\n724\t            \"58%\",\n725\t            \"59%\",\n726\t            \"63%\"\n727\t          ]\n728\t        ]\n729\t      }\n730\t    ],\n731\t    \"figures\": [],\n732\t    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。 Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。 strengthen了\\\"recovery dominates pruning structure\\\"的narrative。\\n\\n\\nBonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%）， 因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%， 与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。 GRPO同样无额外增益。 Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver， pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。 作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\\n\"\n733\t  },\n734\t  {\n735\t    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n736\t    \"description\": \"CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\",\n737\t    \"results\": {\n738\t      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n739\t      \"split_half_p_value\": \"<0.0001\",\n740\t      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation\": 0.96,\n741\t      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.98,\n742\t      \"cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.94,\n743\t      \"cka_score_cv_across_splits\": 0.04\n744\t    },\n745\t    \"tables\": [\n746\t      {\n747\t        \"name\": \"Table 15: CKA Reliability\",\n748\t        \"columns\": [\n749\t          \"Metric\",\n750\t          \"Value\"\n751\t        ],\n752\t        \"rows\": [\n753\t          [\n754\t            \"Split-half Spearman ρ\",\n755\t            \"0.93\"\n756\t          ],\n757\t          [\n758\t            \"Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\",\n759\t            \"0.94\"\n760\t          ],\n761\t          [\n762\t            \"CKA score CV across splits\",\n763\t            \"0.04\"\n764\t          ]\n765\t        ]\n766\t      }\n767\t    ],\n768\t    \"figures\": [],\n769\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility—— 不是因为measurement noise导致CKA不predictive， 而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。 论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\\n\\n\\nCKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration sizes）。 这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的， 问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured property（functional overlap） 与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。 Split-half ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates—— 它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts recovery。 Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\\n\"\n770\t  },\n771\t  {\n772\t    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n773\t    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\",\n774\t    \"results\": {\n775\t      \"alpha_0_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n776\t      \"alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n777\t      \"alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100\": 0.29,\n778\t      \"alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.3,\n779\t      \"alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.34,\n780\t      \"alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.4,\n781\t      \"alpha_optimal\": 4.0,\n782\t      \"alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp\": 12,\n783\t      \"alpha_monotonic\": true,\n784\t      \"alpha_1p0_sft_recovery\": 0.59,\n785\t      \"alpha_4p0_sft_recovery\": 0.62,\n786\t      \"alpha_0_sft_recovery\": 0.64\n787\t    },\n788\t    \"tables\": [\n789\t      {\n790\t        \"name\": \"Table 16: α Ablation Results\",\n791\t        \"columns\": [\n792\t          \"α\",\n793\t          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n794\t          \"Post-SFT GSM8K\",\n795\t          \"Post-SFT→GRPO\"\n796\t        ],\n797\t        \"rows\": [\n798\t          [\n799\t            \"0 (Standard)\",\n800\t            \"28%\",\n801\t            \"64%\",\n802\t            \"63%\"\n803\t          ],\n804\t          [\n805\t            \"0.25\",\n806\t            \"28%\",\n807\t            \"63%\",\n808\t            \"62%\"\n809\t          ],\n810\t          [\n811\t            \"0.5\",\n812\t            \"29%\",\n813\t            \"62%\",\n814\t            \"62%\"\n815\t          ],\n816\t          [\n817\t            \"1.0\",\n818\t            \"30%\",\n819\t            \"59%\",\n820\t            \"60%\"\n821\t          ],\n822\t          [\n823\t            \"2.0\",\n824\t            \"34%\",\n825\t            \"60%\",\n826\t            \"60%\"\n827\t          ],\n828\t          [\n829\t            \"4.0\",\n830\t            \"40%\",\n831\t            \"62%\",\n832\t            \"59%\"\n833\t          ]\n834\t        ]\n835\t      }\n836\t    ],\n837\t    \"figures\": [],\n838\t    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。 Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic improvement up to +12pp）。 Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。 这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。 论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention， 但其mechanism是importance distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。 Post-recovery的non-monotonic pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting） 可能accidentally produce structures that are more SFT-receptive。\\n\\n\\nα=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。 Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的 exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。 但关键反转发生在SFT recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%， α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。 Post-prune advantage（α=4.0 > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转 （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。 这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy） 而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。 RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery—— 因为它over-protects structures that are important but not SFT-recoverable， 同时under-removes structures that are less important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\\n\"\n839\t  },\n840\t  {\n841\t    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n842\t    \"description\": \"Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\",\n843\t    \"results\": {\n844\t      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 28.5,\n845\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 25.2,\n846\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 25.0,\n847\t      \"speedup_rasp_vs_dense\": 1.13,\n848\t      \"speedup_standard_vs_dense\": 1.14,\n849\t      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 35.1,\n850\t      \"rasp_20_throughput\": 39.7,\n851\t      \"standard_20_throughput\": 40.0,\n852\t      \"memory_reduction_percent\": 18.5,\n853\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff\": \"<1%\"\n854\t    },\n855\t    \"tables\": [\n856\t      {\n857\t        \"name\": \"Table 17: Inference Speedup\",\n858\t        \"columns\": [\n859\t          \"Model\",\n860\t          \"Latency (ms/tok)\",\n861\t          \"Throughput (tok/s)\",\n862\t          \"Memory (GB)\"\n863\t        ],\n864\t        \"rows\": [\n865\t          [\n866\t            \"Dense\",\n867\t            \"28.5\",\n868\t            \"35.1\",\n869\t            \"14.2\"\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            \"RASP-20\",\n873\t            \"25.2\",\n874\t            \"39.7\",\n875\t            \"11.6\"\n876\t          ],\n877\t          [\n878\t            \"Standard-20\",\n879\t            \"25.0\",\n880\t            \"40.0\",\n881\t            \"11.5\"\n882\t          ],\n883\t          [\n884\t            \"Speedup vs Dense\",\n885\t            \"1.13×/1.14×\",\n886\t            \"1.13×/1.14×\",\n887\t            \"18.3%/19.0% saved\"\n888\t          ]\n889\t        ]\n890\t      }\n891\t    ],\n892\t    \"figures\": [],\n893\t    \"analysis\": \"Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。 这reinforces worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes （neither accuracy post-recovery nor inference efficiency）。 论文中作为实用性baseline data。\\n\\n\\nStructured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs， 但实际speedup仅~1.13x due to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes 和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。 RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures， 只是选择了不同的specific structures。 Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。 Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期—— 不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured pruning的practical motivation。\\n\"\n894\t  },\n895\t  {\n896\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n897\t    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\",\n898\t    \"results\": {\n899\t      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.56,\n900\t      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.545,\n901\t      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_100\": 0.64,\n902\t      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_100\": 0.65,\n903\t      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319\": 0.635,\n904\t      \"unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp\": -0.5,\n905\t      \"unstructured_speedup_ratio\": 1.02,\n906\t      \"unstructured_memory_saved\": 0\n907\t    },\n908\t    \"tables\": [\n909\t      {\n910\t        \"name\": \"Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison\",\n911\t        \"columns\": [\n912\t          \"Method\",\n913\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n914\t          \"Post-Recovery\",\n915\t          \"Speedup\"\n916\t        ],\n917\t        \"rows\": [\n918\t          [\n919\t            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n920\t            \"54.5%\",\n921\t            \"63.5%\",\n922\t            \"1.02×\"\n923\t          ],\n924\t          [\n925\t            \"RASP-20 (structured)\",\n926\t            \"29.3%\",\n927\t            \"57.8%\",\n928\t            \"1.13×\"\n929\t          ],\n930\t          [\n931\t            \"Standard-20 (structured)\",\n932\t            \"28.1%\",\n933\t            \"63.5%\",\n934\t            \"1.14×\"\n935\t          ],\n936\t          [\n937\t            \"GRASPrune-20 (structured)\",\n938\t            \"7.2%\",\n939\t            \"55.0%\",\n940\t            \"1.13×\"\n941\t          ]\n942\t        ]\n943\t      }\n944\t    ],\n945\t    \"figures\": [],\n946\t    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap： structured pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。 Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured accuracy while providing real speedup。 这进一步supports SFT recovery的power—— 它能overcome 27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%） 到达相同的recovered accuracy。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune accuracy （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。 SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。 GRPO adds 1pp to 65%。 但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map to GPU hardware。 最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable—— structured pruning通过recovery \\\"catches up\\\" to unstructured的保留能力。 这是一个interesting finding for worst档： structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in accuracy， 但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\\n\"\n947\t  },\n948\t  {\n949\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n950\t    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\",\n951\t    \"results\": {\n952\t      \"sft_standard_20_math500\": 0.3,\n953\t      \"sft_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.37,\n954\t      \"sft_rasp_20_math500\": 0.25,\n955\t      \"sft_rasp_20_humaneval\": 0.31,\n956\t      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n957\t      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n958\t      \"standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate\": 0.42,\n959\t      \"rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate\": 0.35,\n960\t      \"standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp\": 5,\n961\t      \"standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp\": 6\n962\t    },\n963\t    \"tables\": [\n964\t      {\n965\t        \"name\": \"Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation\",\n966\t        \"columns\": [\n967\t          \"Model\",\n968\t          \"GSM8K (ID)\",\n969\t          \"MATH-500 (OOD)\",\n970\t          \"HumanEval (OOD)\"\n971\t        ],\n972\t        \"rows\": [\n973\t          [\n974\t            \"Dense\",\n975\t            \"76.4%\",\n976\t            \"52%\",\n977\t            \"58%\"\n978\t          ],\n979\t          [\n980\t            \"Standard-20 + SFT\",\n981\t            \"63.5%\",\n982\t            \"30%\",\n983\t            \"37%\"\n984\t          ],\n985\t          [\n986\t            \"RASP-20 + SFT\",\n987\t            \"55.3%\",\n988\t            \"25%\",\n989\t            \"31%\"\n990\t          ],\n991\t          [\n992\t            \"Δ (Std−RASP)\",\n993\t            \"+8.2pp\",\n994\t            \"+5pp\",\n995\t            \"+6pp\"\n996\t          ]\n997\t        ]\n998\t      }\n999\t    ],\n1000\t    \"figures\": [],\n1001\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is genuine。 论文中这应作为robustness evidence， framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。 Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong representational properties， 可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\\n\\nStandard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%） 是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO： Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。 Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution advantage（+7pp GSM8K）， 说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。 这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一—— 即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。 Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\\n\"\n1002\t  }\n1003\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3676cd4c-b4e1-40d9-b1c2-15aa6f59b21a","uuid":"bcc85efb-ae3b-4f7b-bad6-d082c63cfc9d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:45:46.793Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\",\n    \"description\": \"Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319\": 0.764,\n      \"dense_baseline_ci95\": \"±0.023\",\n      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.293,\n      \"rasp_20_ci95\": \"±0.025\",\n      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.281,\n      \"standard_20_ci95\": \"±0.025\",\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 1.2,\n      \"gap_p_value_bootstrap\": 0.34,\n      \"n_samples\": 1319\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"vs Dense Drop\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense Baseline\",\n            \"76.4%\",\n            \"±2.3pp\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP-20\",\n            \"29.3%\",\n            \"±2.5pp\",\n            \"-47.1pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"±2.5pp\",\n            \"-48.3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ (RASP − Standard)\",\n            \"+1.2pp\",\n            \"\",\n            \"p=0.34\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认）， full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。 这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。 两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。 论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\\n\\n\\nN=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。 扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp， 因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。 RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP groups， 大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set）， 导致full eval下gap不显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT Warmup Recovery\",\n    \"description\": \"SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n      \"sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_gap_pp\": -7,\n      \"sft_rasp_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_standard_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_rasp_token_accuracy\": 0.83,\n      \"sft_standard_token_accuracy\": 0.83,\n      \"eos_rate_both\": 0.99,\n      \"total_steps\": 1870\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: SFT Recovery Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pruned Model\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Recovery Gain\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP-20\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"57%\",\n            \"+28pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"+36pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence： recovery更多取决于training signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。 Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。 这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures， 而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。 两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%）， 说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned model的representational capacity分配上。 关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\",\n    \"description\": \"在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.59,\n      \"grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.63,\n      \"grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp\": 2,\n      \"grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp\": -1,\n      \"grpo_gap_pp\": -4,\n      \"grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final\": 0.42,\n      \"grpo_standard_reward_mean_final\": 0.45,\n      \"training_stable\": true,\n      \"convergence_step\": 800\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\",\n          \"GRPO Gain\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP-20\",\n            \"57%\",\n            \"59%\",\n            \"+2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"63%\",\n            \"-1pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。 这是worst档的decisive evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。 无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。 论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality）， 而非pruning-recovery的structural alignment。\\n\\n\\n已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。 RASP从57%→59%（+2pp marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。 GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable performance， GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。 这与\\\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\\\"的核心假设一致。 Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\",\n    \"description\": \"所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_baseline_1319\": 0.764,\n      \"sft_rasp_20_1319\": 0.553,\n      \"sft_standard_20_1319\": 0.635,\n      \"grpo_rasp_20_1319\": 0.578,\n      \"grpo_standard_20_1319\": 0.621,\n      \"sft_rasp_ci95\": \"±0.027\",\n      \"sft_standard_ci95\": \"±0.026\",\n      \"grpo_rasp_ci95\": \"±0.027\",\n      \"grpo_standard_ci95\": \"±0.026\",\n      \"grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff\": 2.5,\n      \"grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff\": -1.4,\n      \"best_overall\": \"SFT-Standard (63.5%)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pipeline\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-Recovery\",\n          \"Recovery Rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP + SFT\",\n            \"29.3%\",\n            \"55.3%\",\n            \"55.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP + SFT→GRPO\",\n            \"29.3%\",\n            \"57.8%\",\n            \"60.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard + SFT\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"73.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard + SFT→GRPO\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"62.1%\",\n            \"70.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Dense (no pruning)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"76.4%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal—— 比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。 GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR recovery的必要性 （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\\n\\n\\nN=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。 SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT RASP的57%降至55.3%。 GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。 关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。 这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.08,\n      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.072,\n      \"grasp_20_eos_rate\": 0.02,\n      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100\": 0.58,\n      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319\": 0.56,\n      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319\": 0.55,\n      \"grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp\": 50,\n      \"grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp\": -1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Stage\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"Gain from Previous\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Post-Prune\",\n            \"7.2%\",\n            \"-69.2pp from dense\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Post-SFT\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"+48.8pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Post-SFT→GRPO\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"-1.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。 8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability， regardless of which structures were pruned。 这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge： 如果recovery主要由training data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到）， 因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。 但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一： post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。 GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。 这直接反驳了\\\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\\\"的claim—— 即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。 GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_seed42\": 0.293,\n      \"rasp_20_seed123\": 0.285,\n      \"rasp_20_seed456\": 0.301,\n      \"rasp_20_seed789\": 0.278,\n      \"rasp_20_seed1024\": 0.289,\n      \"rasp_20_mean\": 0.289,\n      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.008,\n      \"standard_20_seed42\": 0.281,\n      \"standard_20_seed123\": 0.275,\n      \"standard_20_seed456\": 0.292,\n      \"standard_20_seed789\": 0.269,\n      \"standard_20_seed1024\": 0.283,\n      \"standard_20_mean\": 0.28,\n      \"standard_20_std\": 0.008,\n      \"pairwise_gap_mean_pp\": 0.9,\n      \"pairwise_gap_std\": 0.6,\n      \"paired_t_test_p\": 0.15,\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.19,\n      \"cohens_d\": 0.35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"RASP-20\",\n          \"Standard-20\",\n          \"Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            \"29.3%\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"+1.2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            123,\n            \"28.5%\",\n            \"27.5%\",\n            \"+1.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            456,\n            \"30.1%\",\n            \"29.2%\",\n            \"+0.9pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            789,\n            \"27.8%\",\n            \"26.9%\",\n            \"+0.9pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1024,\n            \"28.9%\",\n            \"28.3%\",\n            \"+0.6pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std\",\n            \"28.9±0.8%\",\n            \"28.0±0.8%\",\n            \"+0.9±0.6pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p-value\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"0.15 (paired-t)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。 论文中应honest report这个null result， 并argue这个negative finding本身有价值： 在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning outcome。\\n\\n\\n5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。 Paired t-test p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。 Cohen's d=0.35属于small effect size。 seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级， 说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。 Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect <1pp的真实差异， 但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_100\": 0.27,\n      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_100\": 0.26,\n      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_100\": 0.14,\n      \"rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100\": 0.4,\n      \"standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n      \"rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100\": 0.3,\n      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.265,\n      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.255,\n      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_1319\": 0.135\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scoring Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n          \"vs Standard Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"14%\",\n            \"-14pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient-only\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"-2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Magnitude-only\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"-1pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard (Wanda I(h))\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP α=1.0\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"+2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP α=4.0\",\n            \"40%\",\n            \"+12pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。 α scaling本质上改变了importance score的distribution shape—— 它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal ones， CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。 为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α without CKA）， 如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。 论文中应将此framed为\\\"α-scaled importance scoring improves pruning\\\"而非\\\"CKA predicts recoverability\\\"。\\n\\n\\nRandom pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order matters。 Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%）， 三种importance-based方法在moderate sparsity下几乎等价。 RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。 关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。 α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应 （α放大了high-overlap groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail）， 而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects regression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mlp_groups\": 784,\n      \"n_pruned_mlp_groups\": 200,\n      \"cka_beta_coefficient\": 0.08,\n      \"cka_beta_p_value\": 0.12,\n      \"cka_incremental_r2\": 0.018,\n      \"weight_norm_beta\": 0.23,\n      \"weight_norm_p\": 0.001,\n      \"gradient_importance_beta\": 0.31,\n      \"gradient_importance_p\": 0.0003,\n      \"activation_magnitude_beta\": 0.19,\n      \"activation_magnitude_p\": 0.004,\n      \"full_model_r2\": 0.34,\n      \"model_without_cka_r2\": 0.32,\n      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.15,\n      \"cka_spearman_with_recoverability\": 0.11,\n      \"cka_spearman_p\": 0.09\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"β\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Incremental R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Gradient Importance\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"0.14\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weight Norm\",\n            \"0.23\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.001\",\n            \"0.09\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Activation Magnitude\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.004\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA Overlap F(h)\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.018\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full Model R²\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"0.34\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。 Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。 论文reframe：functional overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported predictor of recovery outcomes。 Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative result credible且publishable。\\n\\n\\nMixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。 Incremental R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。 相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003） 都是stronger predictors。 CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。 核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity， 但RLVR recovery不是通过\\\"redistribute function across heads\\\"实现的—— RLVR更多是global optimization of the loss landscape， individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive power有限。 Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.57,\n      \"sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.553,\n      \"sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.635,\n      \"sft_only_gap_pp\": -7,\n      \"grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.578,\n      \"grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.621,\n      \"interaction_f_test_p\": 0.41,\n      \"pruning_method_main_effect_p\": 0.03,\n      \"recovery_method_main_effect_p\": 0.62,\n      \"interaction_effect_size\": 0.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"SFT-Only\",\n          \"SFT→GRPO\",\n          \"Δ(GRPO−SFT)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP-20\",\n            \"55.3%\",\n            \"57.8%\",\n            \"+2.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"62.1%\",\n            \"-1.4pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ(Std−RASP)\",\n            \"+8.2pp\",\n            \"+4.3pp\",\n            \"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Effect\",\n          \"F\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"η²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pruning Method\",\n            \"5.12\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recovery Method\",\n            \"0.24\",\n            \"0.62\",\n            \"0.004\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Interaction\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"0.02\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。 Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null interaction。 论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust—— 无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。 这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training signal而非pruning structure。\\n\\n\\nplan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。 2×2 ANOVA (pruning × recovery)显示： pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03）， recovery method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62）， 交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。 这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP， 且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。 Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal pruning order）被直接否定。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\",\n    \"description\": \"25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.18,\n      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.172,\n      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.16,\n      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.155,\n      \"postprune_gap_25_pp\": 1.7,\n      \"rasp_25_post_sft_100\": 0.48,\n      \"standard_25_post_sft_100\": 0.52,\n      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_100\": 0.49,\n      \"standard_25_post_grpo_100\": 0.53,\n      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_1319\": 0.475,\n      \"standard_25_post_grpo_1319\": 0.515,\n      \"recovery_rate_rasp_25\": 0.512,\n      \"recovery_rate_standard_25\": 0.59\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP-25\",\n            \"17.2%\",\n            \"48%\",\n            \"49%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-25\",\n            \"15.5%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"53%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ (RASP−Std)\",\n            \"+1.7pp\",\n            \"-4pp\",\n            \"-4pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better， GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。 论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen negative findings的generality。\\n\\n\\n25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。 RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。 SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。 GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。 关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp）， 说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。 这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择 相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order effect。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n    \"description\": \"30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.05,\n      \"standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.04,\n      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.08,\n      \"rasp_30_avg_len\": 3200,\n      \"standard_30_avg_len\": 3800,\n      \"gap_pp\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"EOS Rate\",\n          \"Avg Length\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP-30\",\n            \"5%\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"3200\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-30\",\n            \"4%\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"3800\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"30% sparsity是\\\"no man's land\\\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful recovery。 两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%） suggests a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\\n\\n\\n30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%）， consistent with已知的35% sparsity完全collapse（D005）。 RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。 EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。 不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。 这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\",\n    \"description\": \"Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n      \"grpo_rasp_20_math500\": 0.24,\n      \"grpo_rasp_20_humaneval\": 0.31,\n      \"grpo_standard_20_math500\": 0.28,\n      \"grpo_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"sft_standard_20_math500\": 0.3,\n      \"sft_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.37,\n      \"rasp_math500_advantage_pp\": -4,\n      \"rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp\": -4,\n      \"math500_recovery_rate_rasp\": 0.36,\n      \"math500_recovery_rate_standard\": 0.46\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 13: OOD Evaluation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH-500\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense Baseline\",\n            \"76.4%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"58%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP-20 + GRPO\",\n            \"57.8%\",\n            \"24%\",\n            \"31%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20 + GRPO\",\n            \"62.1%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"35%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20 + SFT\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"37%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD results消除了\\\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\\\"的concern—— Standard在所有domains上都consistently better。 RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。 论文中：recovery后的OOD degradation是under-explored area， 无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\\n\\n\\nOOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。 Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent—— 不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。 RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware pruning保留的structures 对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。 所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning preservation 对distribution shift很脆弱。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.25,\n      \"bonsai_20_post_sft_100\": 0.59,\n      \"bonsai_20_post_grpo_100\": 0.58,\n      \"bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp\": -3,\n      \"bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp\": -5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 14: Bonsai Baseline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Stage\",\n          \"Bonsai-20\",\n          \"RASP-20\",\n          \"Standard-20\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Post-Prune\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"28%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Post-SFT\",\n            \"59%\",\n            \"57%\",\n            \"64%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Post-GRPO\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"59%\",\n            \"63%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。 Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。 strengthen了\\\"recovery dominates pruning structure\\\"的narrative。\\n\\n\\nBonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%）， 因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%， 与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。 GRPO同样无额外增益。 Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver， pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。 作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n      \"split_half_p_value\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation\": 0.96,\n      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.98,\n      \"cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.94,\n      \"cka_score_cv_across_splits\": 0.04\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 15: CKA Reliability\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Split-half Spearman ρ\",\n            \"0.93\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\",\n            \"0.94\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA score CV across splits\",\n            \"0.04\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility—— 不是因为measurement noise导致CKA不predictive， 而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。 论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\\n\\n\\nCKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration sizes）。 这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的， 问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured property（functional overlap） 与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。 Split-half ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates—— 它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts recovery。 Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpha_0_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n      \"alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100\": 0.28,\n      \"alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100\": 0.29,\n      \"alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.3,\n      \"alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.34,\n      \"alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100\": 0.4,\n      \"alpha_optimal\": 4.0,\n      \"alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp\": 12,\n      \"alpha_monotonic\": true,\n      \"alpha_1p0_sft_recovery\": 0.59,\n      \"alpha_4p0_sft_recovery\": 0.62,\n      \"alpha_0_sft_recovery\": 0.64\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 16: α Ablation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"α\",\n          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n          \"Post-SFT GSM8K\",\n          \"Post-SFT→GRPO\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (Standard)\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"63%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.25\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"63%\",\n            \"62%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.5\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"62%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.0\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"59%\",\n            \"60%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2.0\",\n            \"34%\",\n            \"60%\",\n            \"60%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"40%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"59%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。 Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic improvement up to +12pp）。 Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。 这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。 论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention， 但其mechanism是importance distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。 Post-recovery的non-monotonic pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting） 可能accidentally produce structures that are more SFT-receptive。\\n\\n\\nα=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。 Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的 exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。 但关键反转发生在SFT recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%， α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。 Post-prune advantage（α=4.0 > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转 （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。 这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy） 而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。 RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery—— 因为它over-protects structures that are important but not SFT-recoverable， 同时under-removes structures that are less important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 28.5,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 25.2,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 25.0,\n      \"speedup_rasp_vs_dense\": 1.13,\n      \"speedup_standard_vs_dense\": 1.14,\n      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 35.1,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput\": 39.7,\n      \"standard_20_throughput\": 40.0,\n      \"memory_reduction_percent\": 18.5,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff\": \"<1%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 17: Inference Speedup\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Latency (ms/tok)\",\n          \"Throughput (tok/s)\",\n          \"Memory (GB)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"28.5\",\n            \"35.1\",\n            \"14.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP-20\",\n            \"25.2\",\n            \"39.7\",\n            \"11.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20\",\n            \"25.0\",\n            \"40.0\",\n            \"11.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Speedup vs Dense\",\n            \"1.13×/1.14×\",\n            \"1.13×/1.14×\",\n            \"18.3%/19.0% saved\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。 这reinforces worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes （neither accuracy post-recovery nor inference efficiency）。 论文中作为实用性baseline data。\\n\\n\\nStructured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs， 但实际speedup仅~1.13x due to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes 和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。 RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures， 只是选择了不同的specific structures。 Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。 Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期—— 不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured pruning的practical motivation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100\": 0.56,\n      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.545,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_100\": 0.64,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_100\": 0.65,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319\": 0.635,\n      \"unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp\": -0.5,\n      \"unstructured_speedup_ratio\": 1.02,\n      \"unstructured_memory_saved\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-Recovery\",\n          \"Speedup\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"1.02×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP-20 (structured)\",\n            \"29.3%\",\n            \"57.8%\",\n            \"1.13×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20 (structured)\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"1.14×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune-20 (structured)\",\n            \"7.2%\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"1.13×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap： structured pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。 Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured accuracy while providing real speedup。 这进一步supports SFT recovery的power—— 它能overcome 27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%） 到达相同的recovered accuracy。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune accuracy （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。 SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。 GRPO adds 1pp to 65%。 但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map to GPU hardware。 最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable—— structured pruning通过recovery \\\"catches up\\\" to unstructured的保留能力。 这是一个interesting finding for worst档： structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in accuracy， 但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_standard_20_math500\": 0.3,\n      \"sft_standard_20_humaneval\": 0.37,\n      \"sft_rasp_20_math500\": 0.25,\n      \"sft_rasp_20_humaneval\": 0.31,\n      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n      \"standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate\": 0.35,\n      \"standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp\": 5,\n      \"standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"GSM8K (ID)\",\n          \"MATH-500 (OOD)\",\n          \"HumanEval (OOD)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"76.4%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"58%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard-20 + SFT\",\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"37%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP-20 + SFT\",\n            \"55.3%\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"31%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ (Std−RASP)\",\n            \"+8.2pp\",\n            \"+5pp\",\n            \"+6pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is genuine。 论文中这应作为robustness evidence， framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。 Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong representational properties， 可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\\n\\nStandard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%） 是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO： Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。 Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution advantage（+7pp GSM8K）， 说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。 这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一—— 即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。 Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1003,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1003}}}
